  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 27-year-old woman presents with a 3-month history of fatigue, painful swelling of the small joints of her hands, and a rash over her cheeks and nose bridge that worsens after sun exposure. She also reports intermittent mouth ulcers. Examination shows a malar rash sparing the nasolabial folds and synovitis of the MCP and PIP joints bilaterally. Blood tests show Hb 105 g/L, WCC 3.1 x10^9/L, platelets 118 x10^9/L, and a positive ANA at high titre.',
  'Which further test is most useful to confirm the underlying diagnosis?',
  array['SLE','malar rash','ANA']
),
